# Citation metadata for the GLACE catalog, read by GitHub and by Zenodo when
# the GitHub bridge archives a release (R-16). `version` is one string with
# DATASET_VERSION and the two collection documents; tests/test_version.py
# enforces that. `date-released` is written in the release commit itself.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this dataset, please cite it as below.
type: dataset
title: "GLACE: Sentinel-1 coherence and backscatter composites over Alpine glaciers"
abstract: >-
  A preliminary release covering the glacierised Swiss Alps, published to
  exercise the GLACE publication pipeline while the full dataset is being
  produced: annual summer composites of Sentinel-1 12-day repeat-pass InSAR
  coherence (COH12) and radiometrically terrain-corrected backscatter (RTC),
  2021 onward. Composites are locally resolution weighted, so each output pixel
  is dominated by the acquisitions that resolve it best rather than by whichever
  orbit happened to observe it most often. Two collections are published:
  per-tile composites on the 10 m MGRS grid for analysis and machine learning,
  and one annual mosaic per year on a fixed WebMercator grid for mapping and
  inspection.
authors:
  - family-names: Gentner
    given-names: Luis Q.
    email: luis.gentner@geo.uzh.ch
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4453-0881
    affiliation: University of Zurich, Department of Geography
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: https://github.com/lqgentner/glace-catalog
url: https://data.source.coop/lqgentner/glace-ch
version: "1.0"
keywords:
  - Sentinel-1
  - SAR
  - InSAR coherence
  - backscatter
  - glaciers
  - Alps
  - mosaic
  - cryosphere
